# 13. Audio Capture Architecture

## Overview

The Audio Capture Service is responsible for acquiring audio from the user's environment with minimal latency.

The service is designed as the entry point of the entire AI pipeline.

No business logic exists inside this module.

Its only responsibility is acquiring audio frames and publishing them to the Event Bus.

---

## Design Goals

- Low latency
- High reliability
- Platform abstraction
- Configurable sample rate
- Configurable channels
- Noise tolerant
- Easily replaceable implementation

---

## Supported Audio Sources

Phase 1

- Default microphone

Phase 2

- System audio
- Loopback audio
- Virtual audio devices

Phase 3

- Teams
- Zoom
- Google Meet
- Slack Huddles

The implementation must never depend on a specific meeting application.

---

## Audio Format

Default Sample Rate

16 kHz

Channels

Mono

Encoding

PCM

Chunk Size

Approximately 250 milliseconds

---

## Audio Flow

Microphone

↓

Audio Capture Service

↓

Audio Chunk

↓

Event Bus

↓

Speech Recognition

---

## AudioChunk

Every captured chunk contains:

- session_id
- timestamp
- sample_rate
- duration
- raw_audio
- source
- sequence_number

