# 21. Overlay UI Architecture

## Purpose

The Overlay UI provides real-time assistance without interrupting the user's workflow.

It should feel lightweight, non-intrusive, and always remain secondary to the meeting itself.

The overlay must never block critical meeting content.

---

## Design Principles

- Always on top (optional)
- Minimal visual noise
- Keyboard controllable
- Mouse optional
- Resizable
- Transparent background support
- Draggable
- Theme aware

---

## Overlay Panels

The overlay is composed of independent panels.

Each panel can be enabled or disabled.

Panels include:

- Live Transcript
- Simplified German
- Turkish Translation
- Reply Coach
- Vocabulary
- Action Items
- Meeting Timer
- Confidence Indicator

---

## Panel Independence

Every panel subscribes to events.

Panels never communicate directly.

Example:

Transcript Panel

↓

TranscriptUpdated Event

↓

Panel Refresh

---

Translation Panel

↓

TranslationCompleted Event

↓

Panel Refresh

---

## Layout Modes

Compact Mode

Designed for daily meetings.

Expanded Mode

Shows additional explanations.

Focus Mode

Displays only the most important information.

Learning Mode

Displays progressive hints.

